Third-party notices
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

OpenDraft keeps copyleft dependencies behind process boundaries so that the
core stays under Apache-2.0. See docs/05-interop-license.md for the full
rationale and the boundary design.

* GNU LibreDWG (GPL-3.0-or-later) is NOT linked into this product. DWG support,
  when enabled, runs as the separate executable `od-bridge-dwg`, distributed as
  its own component under GPL-3.0-or-later, communicating over stdio.

* Open CASCADE Technology (LGPL-2.1 with exception), when enabled, is
  dynamically linked. It is an optional dependency and is not required to
  build or run the core.

* IfcOpenShell (LGPL-3.0) is NOT linked into this product in any form. IFC
  export, when enabled, runs as the separate program `od-bridge-ifc`
  (`bridges/od-bridge-ifc`), a standalone Python script distributed as its
  own component, communicating over stdio -- the same process-boundary
  isolation as `od-bridge-dwg`, chosen because IfcOpenShell's only
  supported binding is Python rather than a C library this project could
  link against directly.

